## Implementation Notes

- **cheerio usage**: `const $ = cheerio.load(html); const text = $('body').text();`
- **Truncation strategy**: Take first 2000 chars (don't split mid-word)
  - Better: Truncate at last sentence/period before 2000 chars
- **Domain lookup**: `domainConfig[email.label.toLowerCase()]` (case-insensitive)
- **PII removal**: No explicit PII scrubbing needed (newsletters are public)
  - BUT: Remove email addresses from content if found (privacy for AI)
- **Error handling**: Throw if domain not found in config (fail fast)

## Content Cleaning Examples

**Input**:
```
<p>Hello\r\nWorld</p>\n<script>alert('x')</script>\n\"Important\" news
```

**Output**:
```
Hello World Important news
```

## Security Considerations

- Remove script/style tags (XSS prevention, though not rendering)
- Consider removing email addresses from content before AI (privacy)
- Never send credentials/tokens in content to AI
- Truncate to prevent excessive API costs

